    {
      "id": "1ooeqbo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NON-CONSTITUTIONAL BODIES"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Non-Constitutional bodies are broadly divided into Statutory bodies (created by Acts of Parliament) and Non-Statutory/Executive bodies (created by executive order).",
        "Statutory bodies include key organizations like the National Human Rights Commission (NHRC), Central Vigilance Commission (CVC), Central Information Commission (CIC), and National Green Tribunal (NGT).",
        "NITI Aayog serves as the premier non-statutory executive body acting as a policy think tank for the Government of India.",
        "Constitutional bodies derive their powers directly from the Constitution, whereas non-constitutional bodies derive powers from statutes or executive mandates.",
        "Ongoing reforms are required to enhance the institutional autonomy, effectiveness, and resource allocation of non-constitutional bodies."
      ],
      "id": "z12hz9m"
    },
